  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Preliminary Ecological Appraisal and Protected Species Survey Report, Drainage Assessment Form, Covering Letter, J010-IL-MOGDS1ZZ-004-RP-EN-0001, J010-IL-MOGDS1ZZ-004-DR-EN-0002,  Ground Investigation Report, Planning + Design and Access Statement J010-IL-MOGDS1ZZ-003-DR-TP-0001 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0701 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0702 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0703 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0704 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0705 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0706 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0707 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0708 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0709 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0801 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0802 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0803 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0804 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 0805 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 1301 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 1302 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 1303 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 1304 P01, J010- IL- MOGDS1ZZ- 003- DR- TP- 1305 P01 received 22 April 2022; Site Logistics and Traffic Management Plan, Geotechnical and Geo-Environmental Desk Study J010-DN-MOGD1ZZ-024-RP-C-0001 received 23 June 2022) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The hereby approved CTMP shall be adhered to throughout the construction of the development",
    "Condition : 4 - During the course of the development:\r\na.\tThe Local Planning Authority shall be notified immediately if additional contamination is discovered during the course of the development. A competent person shall assess any such additional contamination, and shall submit appropriate amendments to the scheme for decontamination in writing to the Local Planning Authority for approval before any work on that aspect of development continues.\r\nb.\tSoils or other landscaping materials imported to the site should be demonstrated to be safe for use in accordance with a scheme of verification and testing to be agreed with the local authority.\r\nBefore the development is first brought into use:\r\nc.\tThe agreed scheme for decontamination referred to in clause a) and b) above, including any amendments, shall be fully implemented and a written validation (closure) report submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, a Biodiversity Enhancement Strategy (BES) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details. The BES should include:\r\ni.\tdetails of how the enhancement measures proposed in the Preliminary Ecological Appraisal and Protected Species Survey Report  will be implemented, monitored, managed and maintained, including the long- term design objectives, management responsibilities and maintenance schedules\r\nii.\tadditional detail on location and type of bird/bat boxes, maintenance and a commitment that any data collected is to be shared with the Council;\r\niii.\ta commitment to undertake habitat monitoring annually by a qualified ecologist.\r\n"
  ],
